{"name":"English Walnut","hex":"#3e2b23","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"english","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Spinning or rotary motion given to a ball around the vertical axis, as in pool, billiards or bowling; spin, sidespin.","An unusual or unexpected interpretation of a text or idea, a spin, a nuance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative form of English."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/english"},{"term":"walnut","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hardwood tree of the genus Juglans.","A nut of the walnut tree."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a dark brown colour, the colour of walnut wood."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/walnut"}],"entries":[{"title":"Juglans regia","blocks":[{"text":"Juglans regia, known by various common names including the common walnut, English walnut, or Persian walnut amongst other names, is a species of walnut. It is native to Eurasia in at least southwest and central Asia and southeast Europe, but its exact natural area is obscure due to its long history of cultivation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Noyer_centenaire_en_automne.JPG/330px-Noyer_centenaire_en_automne.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juglans_regia","wikidata":"Q46871"},{"title":"Walnut","blocks":[{"text":"A walnut is the edible seed of any tree of the genus Juglans, most often the Persian or English walnut, Juglans regia. They are accessory fruit because the outer covering of the fruit is technically an involucre and thus not morphologically part of the carpel; this means it cannot be a drupe but is instead a drupe-like nut."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Walnuts_-_whole_and_open_with_halved_kernel.jpg/330px-Walnuts_-_whole_and_open_with_halved_kernel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content